{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Each upon his name.</b> Rashi explained: according to the order of their lineage — the order of the stones: odem for Reuben, pitdah for Simeon, and so for all of them. But according to Rashi's explanation, the name Dan would not be reached there, and in the book of Judges it is written: 'and they called Leshem, Dan, after the name of their father.' And there Rashi explained that Dan's name was written upon Leshem. Therefore there are interpreters who say: 'according to the order of their lineage' means according to the order of the mothers' births — Leah, Bilhah, Zilpah, Rachel — and now Dan's name will be reached there.\n\nHow was it done? Rabbi Yohanan says: they protruded. Resh Lakish says: they were joined together. But the letters tsadi is not written? Rabbi Shimon ben Yohai said: 'Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob' is written there. But the letters tet is not written? Rav Aha bar Yaakov said: 'tribes of Yeshurun' is written there.\n\nAnd in order to write upon each stone six letters, the count of Binyamin, they were written in this order:\n\nאדם פטדה ברקת<br>ראובן א שמעון ב לוי רהם<br>נפך ספיר יהלם<br>יהודה י יששכר צ זבולן ח<br>לשם שבו אחלמה<br>דן ק יעק נפתלי ב גד שבטי<br>תרשיש שהם ישפה<br>אשר ישר יוסף ון בנימין\n\nAnd all the letters total seventy-two letters, corresponding to the seventy-two letters of the explicit Name placed within the choshen."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The text discusses how the tribes' names were engraved on the choshen stones and why certain Hebrew letters appear missing from the acrostic; 'צד״י' and 'טי״ת' refer to the specific Hebrew letters tsadi and tet. The second table segment writes רהם for Levi, which may be a scribal form; translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:59.751824375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}